---
/* Rewritten 2026-09-08. The wording follows how admissions actually describes
   alcohol detox and how callers actually describe their own drinking, rather
   than generic treatment-site prose.

   ⚠ The published copy must never reveal where that wording came from. No
   references to call data, recordings, transcripts or "the calls we take" in
   anything a visitor can read. Keep the voice first-person and ordinary.

   Clinical points that must stay: alcohol is among the more dangerous
   withdrawals, alongside benzodiazepines; there is an anti-seizure protocol for
   alcohol detox; nursing on site around the clock; a physician reviews history
   before arrival.

   The card is the real intake script in the order it is asked. Staff are never
   named in published copy. */
const intake = [
  'When was your last drink?',
  'How much are you drinking in a day?',
  'Can you stop after one or two, or not really?',
  'Do you get tremors, sweating, nausea or vomiting when you stop?',
  'Have you ever had a seizure or blacked out coming off it?',
];
---
<section id="why-detox" class="bg-white py-[60px]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 lg:gap-16 items-start">

      <div>
        <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
          Why supervision helps
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-6">
          Why alcohol detox is safer with medical supervision
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-charcoal text-[17px] leading-[29px]">
          <p>
            The most common version of this call is not a crisis. It is somebody drinking to hold off the shakes: a shot before work, a drink in the morning because stopping physically hurts, or the one that turns into all of them once it starts. If that is where you are, you are not an unusual case here. It is the most ordinary reason people come to us.
          </p>
          <p>
            The reason to do this here rather than at home is straightforward. Alcohol is one of the more dangerous detoxes, and along with benzodiazepines it is one of the two where stopping on your own can genuinely hurt you. That is why there is an anti-seizure protocol for alcohol detox, nursing on site around the clock, and a physician looking at your history before you arrive. It is also why we would rather hear from you before it gets bad enough that making the drive is hard.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">You do not have to be at a particular point to call.</strong> Thirty years or the last six months, daily drinker or weekend binges, one ten-minute conversation settles what the right next step actually is.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-cream rounded-xl p-8 border border-cream-soft border-t-4 border-t-gold lg:sticky lg:top-24">
        <h3 class="font-display text-[24px] leading-[30px] text-navy mb-2">What we will ask you on the phone</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-muted text-[15px] leading-[24px] mb-6">
          The real questions, in the order they come. Nothing here disqualifies anyone.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3.5">
          {intake.map(q => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[26px]">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-gold mt-2.5 shrink-0"></span>
              {q}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-7 pt-6 border-t border-cream-soft">
          <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[26px] mb-4">
            Answering honestly is what lets a provider work out whether you need a detox at all, and how long yours is likely to run.
          </p>
          <a href="tel:8883625576" class="bg-teal hover:bg-teal-dark text-white font-bold px-7 py-3.5 rounded-lg transition-colors font-body tracking-wide inline-block">
            Talk it through with us
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
